This review checks the [original incident](/kb/incidents/4471) against the supplied export,
dated 2026-10-04. It is a snapshot investigation, not a live queue count or an implemented fix.
The counts below come from components running the supplied code and tenant directory.

## One merged ticket conceals different causes

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

**Parser:** the shared parser reads month first although the tenant writes day first.
Harbour Dental's R-41200 describes 7 April becoming 4 July. R-41201 corrects the opposite
direction in a separate report. Day-first app/email reports and booking-v2 form reports
are assigned to this group by the supplied classifier.

**Form hint:** booking-v3 prints MM/DD/YYYY but interprets input in the tenant's day-first
convention. People following that hint can enter a different date than the form reads.
The relevant form reports are from Alder Physio, Copper Studio and Pale Harbour.
R-41230, R-41241 and R-41251 are examples. Fixing the shared parser is not evidence that
this separate hint mismatch is resolved.

<Callout kind="warn">
The classifier's groups are not a complete root-cause diagnosis of every report.
The five one-day-move notes remain counted where the supplied code files them.
Their descriptions, including R-41344's Lisbon/Toronto difference, need separate
investigation. They do not establish a timezone defect or justify a second count.
</Callout>

## Read the timeline correctly

<QueueTimeline ticket={4471} />

Reports received and reports merged are different events. The backlog begins in April;
merging into this ticket begins in July. A merge spike is not evidence of a new failure
starting that week. The chart displays weekly buckets and retains both series.

## Why the existing triage text needs review

The [triage page](/kb/triage/dedupe) and
[accepted decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) describe merging on subject.
Their review date is old enough to trigger the layout's staleness warning. Age is a reason
to check evidence, not automatic proof that a rule is invalid.

The executable examples compare actual causes, with tenant locale, form and channel.
Matching subjects can hide different causes; different subjects can describe the same cause.
Unknown tenants cannot be safely assigned a cause. Browser-locale intake tags can disagree
with the tenant-based classification. Export pagination overlaps, so deduplicate by report ID.

<DedupeExplorer />

## Proposed next steps

- Keep separate engineering tickets for the parser problem and the booking-v3 hint problem.
- Carry the report IDs and export date with each count; recheck counts against fresh data.
- Investigate the five anomalous reports before claiming a complete causal explanation.
- Propose a new decision record for cause-based deduplication. Preserve accepted decision
  0001 unchanged and obtain approval before declaring a replacement policy accepted.
- Reconcile the incident narrative and triage guidance with the reviewed decision and code.

Sources: `src/lib/data/reports-4471.json`, `desk-notes.json`, tenant JSON,
`src/lib/kb/causes.ts`, `locales.ts`, `dedupe-cases.ts`, `staleness.ts`, and the linked pages.
No application fix or policy approval is claimed by this review.

